<report>
<title>Probit analysis - <in>title</in></title>
<p>constant = <in>a</in><br />
slope = <in>b</in></p>

<p>Median * Dose = <in>mxd</in><br />
<ci>Confidence interval <in>het</in> = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></p>

<p>* Dose for centile <in>centile</in> = <in>doseq</in><br />
<ci>Confidence interval <in>het_cent</in> = <in>from_cent</in> to <in>to_cent</in></ci></p>

<p>Chi<sub>2</sub> (heterogeneity of deviations from model) = <in>dev</in>  (<in>df</in> df)  <pval><inp>p</inp></pval></p>

<p>t for slope = <in>t_slope</in> (<in>df</in> df_slope)  <pval><inp>p_slope</inp></pval></p>
<block name="warn">
<p><warn>WARNING: slope not significant</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
